<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taichung</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taichung is a city in central-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and one of its largest municipalities. In the 17th century the plains of the area were home to indigenous peoples such as the Pazeh and Papora. The Qing government began building a provincial capital there in the late 1880s, and under Japanese rule from 1895 it grew into a planned modern city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taichung.jpg" alt="Taichung" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 毛貓大少爺 from Taipei, Taiwan · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Taichung_skyline.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
